.TH GTDO 1 "{{.Date}}" "gtdo {{.Version}}" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtdo \- a Go port of the todo.txt-cli (todo.sh) command line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtdo
.RI [ options ]
.B action
.RI [ task_number ]
.RI [ task_description ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtdo
is a Go port of
.BR todo.txt-cli ,
the todo.sh command line interface for maintaining todo lists in
.IR todo.txt
format: one task per line, optionally tagged with a priority
.RI ((A) ),
a creation date, and
.B @context
and
.B +project
tags.
.PP
Output, prompts, and exit codes match todo.sh byte for byte for the twenty
ported todo.sh actions. Configuration follows todo.sh: command line options,
environment variables, and a configuration file.
.PP
Shell completion is built in: the
.B completion
command generates completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, and powershell,
and the actions complete task numbers and
.B @context
and
.B +project
tags from the current
.IR todo.txt
file.
.PP
As an additional gtdo extension, the
.B format [FILE]
action rewrites both configured task files, or the selected file when
.I FILE
is specified.
{{.Commands}}
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-@
Hide context names in list output.  Use twice to show context names (default).
.TP
.B \-+
Hide project names in list output.  Use twice to show project names (default).
.TP
.B \-c
Color mode
.TP
.BI \-d " CONFIG_FILE"
Use a configuration file other than one of the defaults
.TP
.B \-f
Forces actions without confirmation or interactive input
.TP
.B \-h
Display a short help message; same as action "shorthelp"
.TP
.B \-p
Plain mode turns off colors
.TP
.B \-P
Hide priority labels in list output.  Use twice to show priority labels (default).
.TP
.B \-a
Don't auto-archive tasks automatically on completion
.TP
.B \-A
Auto-archive tasks automatically on completion
.TP
.B \-n
Don't preserve line numbers; automatically remove blank lines on task deletion
.TP
.B \-N
Preserve line numbers
.TP
.B \-t
Prepend the current date to a task automatically when it's added.
.TP
.B \-T
Do not prepend the current date to a task automatically when it's added.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode turns on confirmation messages
.TP
.B \-vv
Extra verbose mode prints some debugging information and additional help text
.TP
.B \-V
Displays version and build information
.TP
.B \-x
No-op; accepted for compatibility with todo.txt-cli
.SH CONFIGURATION
gtdo reads configuration from TOML files.  The following keys are TOML-only;
they have no environment-variable or command-line equivalents.
.TP
.B allowed_contexts
An array of complete context tokens, such as
.BR @work
and
.BR @home .
When this key is omitted, contexts are unrestricted.  An explicit empty array
rejects every context tag.  Matching is exact and case-sensitive.
.TP
.B allowed_projects
An array of complete project tokens, such as
.BR +gtdo
and
.BR +personal .
When this key is omitted, projects are unrestricted.  An explicit empty array
rejects every project tag.  Matching is exact and case-sensitive.
.PP
gtdo validates final task text for
.BR add ,
.BR addm ,
.BR addto ,
.BR append ,
.BR prepend ,
and
.BR replace .
Listing remains usable for legacy tasks with tags that are not allowed.
On rejection, the diagnostic includes the file and 1-based line number, for
example:
.BR "TODO: Context \"@home\" is not allowed in /path/to/todo.txt at line 3."
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TODO_DIR
Path to the directory that holds the todo files.
.TP
.B TODO_FILE
Path to the todo.txt file.
.TP
.B DONE_FILE
Path to the done.txt file.
.TP
.B REPORT_FILE
Path to the report.txt file.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_AUTO_ARCHIVE
Same as option \-a (0) or \-A (1).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_FORCE=1
Same as option \-f.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PRESERVE_LINE_NUMBERS
Same as option \-n (0) or \-N (1).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PLAIN
Same as option \-p (1) or \-c (0).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_DATE_ON_ADD
Same as option \-t (1) or \-T (0).
.TP
.B TODOTXT_PRIORITY_ON_ADD=pri
Default priority A\-Z.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_VERBOSE=1
Same as option \-v.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_DEFAULT_ACTION=""
Run this when called with no arguments.
.TP
.B TODOTXT_SOURCEVAR=$DONE_FILE
Use another source for listcon, listproj.
.TP
.B SENTENCE_DELIMITERS=,.:;
Suppress the added space in append.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B [behavior] task_format
Controls the field order used by the
.B format
action. The default is
.BR [checked][priority][uuid][content][keywords][project][context] .
The formatter inserts one space between non-empty fields automatically. The
available fields are
.BR checked ,
.BR priority ,
.BR uuid ,
.BR content ,
.BR keywords ,
.BR project ,
and
.BR context .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/todo.txt
The active todo list; defaults to
.IR ~/todo.txt .
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/done.txt
Completed tasks; defaults to
.IR ~/done.txt .
.TP
.I $TODO_DIR/report.txt
The report output; defaults to
.IR ~/report.txt .
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtdo/config.toml
User configuration, searched after the
.B \-d
option and
.BR $GTDO_CONFIG ,
before
.IR /etc/gtdo/config.toml .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic error: usage errors, unknown actions, and action failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The todo.txt format: https://github.com/todotxt/todo.txt
.PP
The todo.txt-cli project: https://github.com/todotxt/todo.txt-cli
